{
 "id": "lighting.scene",
 "label": "Light",
 "description": "The light in a scene, described as light: its quality, direction, color and strength, the time of day and the weather. It names no lamp, screen or fixture; the only sources it names (sun, moon, a window, candlelight, lamplight) are ones nearly any such scene has.",
 "pos": "noun phrase",
 "frame": "lit by ___",
 "notes": "The default list for a light slot that names no particular look ('light', 'lighting', 'soft light'). Variety is in mood, time and direction, not in fixtures: a fixture drawn as a light seed was written into the scene as a prop and often didn't belong there (a TV in a restaurant, track lights at a seaside bistro). lighting.indoor_practical owns the fixtures, for slots whose words ask for one. Window, candle and lamp light are indoor; sun and sky looks need a time of day that has them. The slot's narrowing reads the whole scene, so a look the place can't have is left out.",
 "facets": [
  "space",
  "time_of_day"
 ],
